{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":8920,"output":5631,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3937,"totalTokens":14551,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Let me review each item.\n\nQ021: source \"which you do not understand: ...\" target \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解：...\" — source says \"which you do not understand\"; target says \"even if you understand this language, you cannot understand\". That's a contradiction — DIRECTION/CONDITION reversal. FINDING. Target span \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\". Correction: \"你无法理解这种语言：\". Evidence \"which you do not understand\".\n\nQ022: source \"The staff will allow us to drain...\" target \"这根法杖将让我们得以...\" fine. Source context has \"The staff has allowed us...\" but source is \"will allow\". Target matches source. \"You cannot stop us now!\" target \"你现在已经无法阻止我们了！\" fine. Source_context differs but source is the item's source; translation matches source. No finding. Actually the source says \"will allow us\" and target \"将让我们得以\" — fine. No issue.\n\nQ023: source \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" target \"一副狂乱的眼睛凝视着他\" — \"peer out\" means look out through the slot; target says 凝视着他 (stares at him). Also \"他\" — should be \"你\"? The speaker addresses the player: \"What do you want\". Eyes peer out at the player. Target \"凝视着他\" uses third person \"him\" but should be looking out / at you. Is this a defect? \"peer out\" = 看出来/向外窥视. Target \"凝视着他\" — direction/referent: eyes peer out (from inside), not staring at him specifically... Actually peering out through the slot toward the player implies looking at you. \"他\" vs implied \"你\" — in Chinese translation, using \"他\" for player viewpoint is odd. This is arguably SUBJECT/REFERENT issue: player character should be second person. The rest of the translation uses 你 (\"你想干什么\"). So \"凝视着他\" is inconsistent — eyes peer out, staring at him. Hmm. The source \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" doesn't specify whom they look at, just \"peer out\" (向外看). Target adds \"凝视着他\" — the \"他\" contradicts second-person narration. I'd call FINDING REFERENT: correction \"*一副狂乱的眼睛向外窥视。*\" Evidence \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\". Verdict: FINDING seems reasonable since \"他\" is third person while game addresses player as 你.\n\nQ024: \"Aeryn, are you well?\" → \"艾琳，你还好么？\" Fine. No issue.\n\nQ025: source \"I have not been able to find all of the orbs of command in my travels; could you have some of your men search for me?\" target \"我没能找到所有的指令水晶球；请问你可以让你们的人来帮我寻找一下吗？\" — fine. \"orbs of command\" translated \"指令水晶球\" — addition of 水晶? \"orbs\" = 球体, adding 水晶 (crystal) is added info but plausible/compatible? Rule 3: 新增但与可见证据相容、且无法由可见证据判错的具体信息，不构成缺陷. Can visible evidence judge \"水晶\" wrong? Source just says \"orbs\". Can't judge wrong. Not a defect. No finding.\n\nQ026: \"Number of items to make\" → \"制作的物品数量\". Fine.\n\nQ027: source \"Excellent. Return in a few days, and I'll have everything prepared.\" Target: \"很好，几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了。\" Hmm — \"I'll have everything prepared\" future; target \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" reads as already prepared? Ambiguous. Also \"which the men of Sholtar sealed many years ago\" — \"那是多年前肖尔塔人封印的地方\" fine. \"return with it and your odds of surviving our portal attempt will go up drastically\" — \"请帮我带回来，这能大大提高你通过传送门时存活的几率\" fine. The \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — could read \"I'll surely have everything prepared (by then)\". Chinese \"几天后你回来，我肯定把一切都准备好了\" — with 了 it implies completion; future perfect, acceptable. Marginal; I might flag UNCERTAIN on VALUE/TIMING? Actually \"Return in a few days\" — target \"几天后你回来\" fine. I'll say no finding, or UNCERTAIN. I think it's acceptable; skip.\n\nQ028: \"you are called to serve\" → \"你效力的时候到了\" fine-ish. \"The nearby unhallowed morass inhabitants are growing restless\" → \"附近不洁沼泽中的居民正在蠢蠢欲动\" fine. \"You must go there and find the source\" → \"你必须去那里，找到这一切的源头\" fine. No finding.\n\nQ029: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" → \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\" — \"nothing but hatchlings\" means only hatchlings (we've found nothing except hatchlings). Target says \"从未遇上幼龙\" = never encountered hatchlings — opposite! Wait: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" = only hatchlings so far. Target: \"从未遇上幼龙\" (never met hatchlings). That's a VALUE/DIRECTION reversal. FINDING. Target span \"到目前为止从未遇上幼龙\". Correction: \"到目前为止只遇到幼龙\". Evidence \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\".\n\nAlso \"she is something special in combat\" — \"她在战斗中确实不同凡响\" fine. \"wyrmic\" translated 龙战士 fine. \"Expedition Captain\" fine. \"Gorran is one of the finest rangers I know\" — \"高岚是我认识的最优秀的巡林客之一\" fine. No other findings.\n\nQ030: \"Report for bad behavior\" → \"举报我的不良行为\" — wait, this is a menu option to report another user's bad behavior. \"我的\" (my) is wrong — the report is about the other user. Source context: user menu for another player (citem.login), option \"Report for bad behavior\" ui=\"report\". Target adds \"我的\" making it report my own behavior. SUBJECT/REFERENT error. FINDING. Correction: \"举报不良行为\" or \"举报该用户的不良行为\". Evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\".\n\nQ031: \"Place the object where?\" → \"将物品丢弃到哪里？\" — source context shows options include inventory and drop; \"place\" ≠ only \"drop\". Target narrows to 丢弃 (drop). But wait — rule: if source_context exists, it's equally valid evidence. Context shows the dialog offers \"Inventory of %s\", \"Drop @\", \"NPC Inventory\". So \"丢弃\" is wrong — should be \"放置\". FINDING. Target span \"将物品丢弃到哪里\". Evidence \"Place the object where?\" Correction: \"将物品放到哪里？\".\n\nQ032: source \"Amassed 3000 gold pieces.\" target \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" — the target adds \"在'龙之贪婪'成就中\" (in the Dragon's Greed achievement). Source context shows this desc belongs to \"Treasure Hoarder\" achievement (3000), while Dragon's Greed is 8000. So the addition is contradicted by source context — the achievement is Treasure Hoarder, not Dragon's Greed. FINDING (ADDITION/REFERENT). Target span \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币\" — actually span must appear verbatim: \"在\"龙之贪婪\"成就中积累3000金币。\" The quotes are Chinese full-width \"龙之贪婪\". In the target JSON: \"在“龙之贪婪”成就中积累3000金币。\" I must reproduce exactly. Evidence: source_context shows name = \"Treasure Hoarder\" with desc [[SOURCE_MATCH_1]] and can_gain 3000, while DRAGON_GREED desc is \"Amassed 8000 gold pieces.\" Evidence string must appear verbatim in source or source_context. Use \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" — appears in context. Correction: \"积累3000金币。\" Good.\n\nQ033: \"Became the new master of the arena in 30-wave mode.\" → \"在30波模式中成为新的竞技场主宰。\" Fine.\n\nQ034: \"I will not let you down!\" → \"我一定会让你失望的！\" — opposite meaning! FINDING. Correction: \"我不会让你失望的！\" Claim type DIRECTION (negation reversal) or VALUE. I'll use DIRECTION.\n\nQ035: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" → \"竞技场生存至第20轮。\" — 50 vs 20. FINDING VALUE. Correction \"竞技场生存至第50轮。\" Evidence \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\"\n\nQ036: \"Now, this is impressive!\" — this is an achievement NAME (LINANIIL_DEAD). Target \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — adds \"这个发现\" (this discovery). Source doesn't mention discovery. Is that a defect? Achievement name as exclamation. \"Now, this is impressive!\" Target adds discovery — addition of info not in source. Can visible evidence judge it wrong? Source is just an exclamation; \"这个发现\" adds a specific referent. Hmm, achievement is for killing Linaniil... \"发现\" is not supported. But rule 3: new info compatible with visible evidence and can't be judged wrong by visible evidence doesn't constitute defect. Is \"这个发现\" judgeable as wrong? The source is an exclamation without referent; adding \"发现\" introduces an element not present. It's an ADDITION of a specific subject. I could report as FINDING ADDITION or UNCERTAIN. Given it's an achievement name, adding \"这个发现\" changes meaning somewhat. I'd say FINDING ADDITION: correction \"哇，这可真令人印象深刻！\" Evidence \"Now, this is impressive!\". Hmm, but is that objective? The source has no mention of discovery; the translation asserts \"this discovery\" — objectively an added noun. I'll go FINDING. Or UNCERTAIN to be safe. Achievement name for killing a boss — \"发现\" is unrelated; I'll say FINDING with claim ADDITION.\n\nQ037: \"Achieved your wild dreams of power and eternal life: you turned into a Lich!\" → \"成就你的野心并获得永恒的生命，你终于成为了巫妖！\" — \"wild dreams of power\" = 对力量的狂野梦想; target \"成就你的野心\" loses \"power\" but okay-ish. \"eternal life\" 永恒的生命 fine. Omission of \"力量\" — minor. \"wild\" dropped. Is that an objective defect? \"dreams of power and eternal life\" → \"野心\" covers power-ish ambition loosely. Marginal; I'd not report. Actually \"power\" omitted: OMISSION. Hmm. 野心 (ambition) partially captures \"dreams of power\". I think it's acceptable paraphrase. Skip.\n\nQ038: \"Kickin' it old-school\" → \"现代风格\" (modern style) — opposite! Old-school = 复古/老派. FINDING. Correction: \"复古怀旧\" / \"老派风格\". Claim DIRECTION or VALUE. Evidence \"Kickin' it old-school\". Target span \"现代风格\".\n\nQ039: \"Killed a boss while already dead.\" → \"在已死亡的状态下杀死一个BOSS。\" Fine. Context: p.dead — party leader dead while killing boss. Fine.\n\nQ040: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" → \"控制次元浮岛使其稳定在地面上。\" — \"maintain it in orbit\" = 保持其在轨道上; target \"稳定在地面上\" (stable on the ground) — contradicts orbit. FINDING. Correction: \"稳定'恍惚穹域'使其维持在轨道上。\" Achievement name \"Orbituary\" supports orbit. Evidence \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" Target span \"使其稳定在地面上\". Claim VALUE/OTHER. Use VALUE? It's about location/state. STATE maybe. I'll use STATE.\n\nAlso Q040 \"Abashed Expanse\" translated \"次元浮岛\" — proper noun; zone name. Can't judge without knowledge? The name \"Abashed Expanse\" ≠ 次元浮岛 (dimensional floating island). But it's a proper noun translation choice; the context shows zone name \"Abashed Expanse\". 次元浮岛 doesn't correspond literally but is a localization choice for the zone. Can't definitively say wrong. Skip.\n\nQ022 check again: source \"will allow us\" target \"将让我们得以\" ok. Also \"summon Him through!\" target \"召唤他降临\" fine. No finding.\n\nQ027: also \"It opens the ruins of Telmur\" — \"它可以打开泰尔玛废墟\" fine. \"your odds of surviving our portal attempt\" — \"你通过传送门时存活的几率\" — \"our portal attempt\" = 我们尝试开启传送门; target \"你通过传送门时\" implies passing through. Slight shift but compatible. Skip. Actually \"我肯定把一切都准备好了\" vs \"I'll have everything prepared\" — future promise. The 了 + 肯定 reads like \"I'll surely have it all ready (by then)\". Acceptable. Skip.\n\nQ023 second thought: is \"凝视着他\" a FINDING? The narration in game is second person (\"What do you want, @playerdescriptor.race@?\"). The slot opens and eyes peer out — at the player. \"凝视着他\" introduces third-person \"him\" inconsistent with the second-person address. Also \"peer out\" (向外看/窥视) vs \"凝视\" (stare). Objective: \"他\" has no antecedent in second-person dialogue; the source's \"peer out\" doesn't specify object. I'll report FINDING REFERENT with correction \"*一副狂乱的眼睛向外窥视。*\". Evidence \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\".\n\nQ026 fine.\n\nQ029: also \"Expedition Captain\" — target \"探险队队长\" placed before name: \"探险队队长，科纳克人战士瑞丽\" fine. \"cornac fighter\" fine.\n\nQ028: \"you are called to serve\" — \"你效力的时候到了\" fine.\n\nNow assemble JSON with 20 items Q021–Q040 in order, observation field required for each.\n\nObservations: brief neutral description.\n\nQ021: FINDING, CONDITION (reversal) — actually type: \"which you do not understand\" → \"即使你懂得\" reverses condition. claim_type CONDITION. Correction: \"你无法理解这种语言：\".\n\nQ022: no candidates, observation.\n\nQ023: FINDING REFERENT.\n\nQ024: none.\n\nQ025: none.\n\nQ026: none.\n\nQ027: none.\n\nQ028: none.\n\nQ029: FINDING DIRECTION (or VALUE). \"Nothing but hatchlings\" = only hatchlings; target negates. I'll use DIRECTION.\n\nQ030: FINDING SUBJECT (target says \"my\" bad behavior). Claim SUBJECT.\n\nQ031: FINDING ACTION (place→drop only). Or SCOPE. I'll use ACTION.\n\nQ032: FINDING ADDITION (achievement name) — actually wrong referent: attributes to Dragon's Greed instead of Treasure Hoarder. REFERENT. Use REFERENT.\n\nQ033: none.\n\nQ034: FINDING DIRECTION.\n\nQ035: FINDING VALUE.\n\nQ036: FINDING ADDITION (or UNCERTAIN). I'll go FINDING ADDITION. Hmm, let me reconsider: \"Now, this is impressive!\" as achievement name for killing Linaniil. Target \"这个发现可真是令人印象深刻！\" — \"这个发现\" is an added subject. Objective enough. FINDING ADDITION, correction \"这可真是令人印象深刻！\".\n\nQ037: none.\n\nQ038: FINDING DIRECTION/VALUE — \"old-school\" → \"现代风格\" reversal. DIRECTION.\n\nQ039: none.\n\nQ040: FINDING STATE (in orbit vs on ground).\n\nFor Q032 evidence: must be verbatim from source_context. \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" appears. Also \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" appears. I'll use: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\"\" plus maybe \"desc = _t[[Amassed 8000 gold pieces.]]\" — evidence can be a single string; I'll include one: \"name = \\\"Treasure Hoarder\\\",\" — check verbatim in context: `\\tname = \"Treasure Hoarder\",` yes contains `name = \"Treasure Hoarder\",`. Good.\n\nFor Q021 evidence: \"which you do not understand:\" verbatim in source. Yes.\n\nFor Q031 evidence: \"Place the object where?\" verbatim in source. Yes. Could also cite \"Drop @\" from context. Use source text.\n\nFor Q040 evidence: \"Stabilized the Abashed Expanse to maintain it in orbit.\" verbatim. Yes.\n\nQ036 evidence: \"Now, this is impressive!\" verbatim.\n\nQ023 evidence: \"a pair of wild eyes peer out\" verbatim.\n\nQ029 evidence: \"Nothing but hatchlings so far\" verbatim.\n\nQ030 evidence: \"Report for bad behavior\" verbatim. Could add context that it's a menu for another user, but evidence must be verbatim string. Use source.\n\nQ034 evidence: \"I will not let you down!\" verbatim.\n\nQ035 evidence: \"Got to wave 50 in the arena.\" verbatim.\n\nQ038 evidence: \"Kickin' it old-school\" verbatim.\n\nTarget spans verbatim:\nQ021: \"即使你懂得这种语言，也无法理解\"\nQ023: